{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0997"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge music-stage/pop-rock","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/music-stage__pop-rock.g2.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",642],["+","Berlin added a festival without a field, and without guitars. The Love Parade began in July 1989 in West Berlin, a few months before the Wall fell, when the DJ Dr. Motte (Matthias Roeingh) and Danielle de Picciotto led about 150 ravers through the city behind a sound truck. It was registered as a political demonstration, and its first motto was „Friede, Freude, Eierkuchen“ – „Peace, Joy, Pancakes“ – standing for disarmament, music and a fair share of food. In the 1990s the techno parade grew into a mass event of hundreds of thousands, later moved to the Ruhr, where Dortmund officially counted 1.6 million people in 2008, and ended for good after the crowd crush in Duisburg on 24 July 2010, in which 21 people died.\n\n"],["=",12],["-","pedals."],["+","pedals"],["=",1],["+","or drum machines. "],["=",268],["+","Love Parade | Berlin (later the Ruhr) | 1989–2010 |\n| "],["=",20],["-","five"],["+","six"],["=",104]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",590],["+","Berlin steuerte ein Festival ohne Acker und ohne Gitarren bei. Die Loveparade begann im Juli 1989 in West-Berlin, wenige Monate vor dem Mauerfall, als der DJ Dr. Motte (Matthias Roeingh) und Danielle de Picciotto rund 150 Raver hinter einem Lautsprecherwagen durch die Stadt führten. Sie war als politische Demonstration angemeldet, und ihr erstes Motto lautete „Friede, Freude, Eierkuchen“ – es stand für Abrüstung, Musik und eine gerechte Verteilung der Nahrung. In den 1990er-Jahren wuchs die Techno-Parade zu einem Massenereignis mit Hunderttausenden heran, zog später ins Ruhrgebiet, wo Dortmund 2008 offiziell 1,6 Millionen Menschen zählte, und endete endgültig nach dem Gedränge in Duisburg am 24. Juli 2010, bei dem 21 Menschen starben.\n\n"],["=",12],["+","oder Drumcomputern "],["=",272],["+","Loveparade | Berlin (später Ruhrgebiet) | 1989–2010 |\n| "],["=",16],["-","fünf"],["+","sechs"],["=",96]]}]},
